# LF everywhere, in the repository AND in every working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The migration runner hashes each .sql file's bytes and refuses to run when an already-applied
# migration has changed. With Git's autocrlf on Windows, a plain checkout rewrites those files to CRLF, every checksum
# changes, and the runner correctly refuses to migrate - "migration 0005 was modified after being applied". The same
# applies to shell scripts, which a CRLF checkout makes unrunnable inside containers and WSL.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
